{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788191101437,"sessionID":"ses_fa78189c6ffeHzmdRAYto1hSK7","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_NJOBNg66HTMSQxmuAivVoEv6","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/in/db/migration_policy.md"},"output":"<path>/workspace/in/db/migration_policy.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Migration Policy\n2: \n3: The migration must preserve existing users and dependent order rows.\n4: \n5: Dirty email cleanup rules:\n6: - Keep the first existing `ada@example.com` row unchanged.\n7: - The duplicate user `u4` must become `ada+u4@example.com`.\n8: - The null email user `u5` must become `missing+u5@example.invalid`.\n9: - The blank email user `u6` must become `missing+u6@example.invalid`.\n10: - Future writes must reject duplicate or null emails.\n11: \n12: Schema rules:\n13: - Add `users.status TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'active'`.\n14: - Preserve historical `created_at`.\n15: - Preserve `orders.user_id` references to the same user ids.\n16: - The migration should run in an explicit transaction and be safe to run twice.\n17: \n18: Rollback:\n19: - `rollback.sql` must execute after the migration.\n20: - It must restore the pre-migration users schema shape: `id`, `email`, `name`, `created_at`.\n21: - It must preserve the same number of user rows and order rows, including dependent orders for dirty users.\n\n(End of file - total 21 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Migration Policy\n\nThe migration must preserve existing users and dependent order rows.\n\nDirty email cleanup rules:\n- Keep the first existing `ada@example.com` row unchanged.\n- The duplicate user `u4` must become `ada+u4@example.com`.\n- The null email user `u5` must become `missing+u5@example.invalid`.\n- The blank email user `u6` must become `missing+u6@example.invalid`.\n- Future writes must reject duplicate or null emails.\n\nSchema rules:\n- Add `users.status TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'active'`.\n- Preserve historical `created_at`.\n- Preserve `orders.user_id` references to the same user ids.\n- The migration should run in an explicit transaction and be safe to run twice.\n\nRollback:\n- `rollback.sql` must execute after the migration.\n- It must restore the pre-migration users schema shape: `id`, `email`, `name`, `created_at`.","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/workspace/in/db/migration_policy.md","text":"# Migration Policy\n\nThe migration must preserve existing users and dependent order rows.\n\nDirty email cleanup rules:\n- Keep the first existing `ada@example.com` row unchanged.\n- The duplicate user `u4` must become `ada+u4@example.com`.\n- The null email user `u5` must become `missing+u5@example.invalid`.\n- The blank email user `u6` must become `missing+u6@example.invalid`.\n- Future writes must reject duplicate or null emails.\n\nSchema rules:\n- Add `users.status TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'active'`.\n- Preserve historical `created_at`.\n- Preserve `orders.user_id` references to the same user ids.\n- The migration should run in an explicit transaction and be safe to run twice.\n\nRollback:\n- `rollback.sql` must execute after the migration.\n- It must restore the pre-migration users schema shape: `id`, `email`, `name`, `created_at`.\n- It must preserve the same number of user rows and order rows, including dependent orders for dirty users.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":21,"totalLines":21,"truncated":false}},"title":"workspace/in/db/migration_policy.md","time":{"start":1788191101413,"end":1788191101434}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_0efdc0a084910d3d016a95a17cc82487d28df23247ff849d06"}},"id":"prt_0587ed0f6001rhjZftXtpFU1NY","sessionID":"ses_fa78189c6ffeHzmdRAYto1hSK7","messageID":"msg_0587ebdcc001EkmW35vNF6hgwr"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788191101910,"sessionID":"ses_fa78189c6ffeHzmdRAYto1hSK7","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_AahimXPnBgN2Gh5iool2auKY","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/in/db/schema.sql"},"output":"<path>/workspace/in/db/schema.sql</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: PRAGMA foreign_keys = ON;\n2: \n3: CREATE TABLE users (\n4:     id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,\n5:     email TEXT,\n6:     name TEXT NOT NULL,\n7:     created_at TEXT NOT NULL\n8: );\n9: \n10: INSERT INTO users (id, email, name, created_at) VALUES\n11: ('u1', 'ada@example.com', 'Ada', '2024-01-02T10:00:00Z'),\n12: ('u2', 'lin@example.com', 'Lin', '2024-02-03T11:30:00Z'),\n13: ('u3', 'grace@example.com', 'Grace', '2024-03-04T09:15:00Z'),\n14: ('u4', 'ada@example.com', 'Ada Legacy', '2023-12-01T08:00:00Z'),\n15: ('u5', NULL, 'Null Email Legacy', '2023-11-05T12:00:00Z'),\n16: ('u6', '', 'Blank Email Legacy', '2023-10-06T07:45:00Z');\n17: \n18: CREATE TABLE orders (\n19:     id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,\n20:     user_id TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES users(id),\n21:     total_cents INTEGER NOT NULL,\n22:     created_at TEXT NOT NULL\n23: );\n24: \n25: INSERT INTO orders (id, user_id, total_cents, created_at) VALUES\n26: ('o1', 'u1', 1299, '2024-04-01T09:00:00Z'),\n27: ('o2', 'u4', 4599, '2024-04-02T10:30:00Z'),\n28: ('o3', 'u5', 799, '2024-04-03T11:45:00Z'),\n29: ('o4', 'u6', 1599, '2024-04-04T12:10:00Z');\n\n(End of file - total 29 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"PRAGMA foreign_keys = ON;\n\nCREATE TABLE users (\n    id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,\n    email TEXT,\n    name TEXT NOT NULL,\n    created_at TEXT NOT NULL\n);\n\nINSERT INTO users (id, email, name, created_at) VALUES\n('u1', 'ada@example.com', 'Ada', '2024-01-02T10:00:00Z'),\n('u2', 'lin@example.com', 'Lin', '2024-02-03T11:30:00Z'),\n('u3', 'grace@example.com', 'Grace', '2024-03-04T09:15:00Z'),\n('u4', 'ada@example.com', 'Ada Legacy', '2023-12-01T08:00:00Z'),\n('u5', NULL, 'Null Email Legacy', '2023-11-05T12:00:00Z'),\n('u6', '', 'Blank Email Legacy', '2023-10-06T07:45:00Z');\n\nCREATE TABLE orders (\n    id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,\n    user_id TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES users(id),","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/workspace/in/db/schema.sql","text":"PRAGMA foreign_keys = ON;\n\nCREATE TABLE users (\n    id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,\n    email TEXT,\n    name TEXT NOT NULL,\n    created_at TEXT NOT NULL\n);\n\nINSERT INTO users (id, email, name, created_at) VALUES\n('u1', 'ada@example.com', 'Ada', '2024-01-02T10:00:00Z'),\n('u2', 'lin@example.com', 'Lin', '2024-02-03T11:30:00Z'),\n('u3', 'grace@example.com', 'Grace', '2024-03-04T09:15:00Z'),\n('u4', 'ada@example.com', 'Ada Legacy', '2023-12-01T08:00:00Z'),\n('u5', NULL, 'Null Email Legacy', '2023-11-05T12:00:00Z'),\n('u6', '', 'Blank Email Legacy', '2023-10-06T07:45:00Z');\n\nCREATE TABLE orders (\n    id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,\n    user_id TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES users(id),\n    total_cents INTEGER NOT NULL,\n    created_at TEXT NOT NULL\n);\n\nINSERT INTO orders (id, user_id, total_cents, created_at) VALUES\n('o1', 'u1', 1299, '2024-04-01T09:00:00Z'),\n('o2', 'u4', 4599, '2024-04-02T10:30:00Z'),\n('o3', 'u5', 799, '2024-04-03T11:45:00Z'),\n('o4', 'u6', 1599, '2024-04-04T12:10:00Z');","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":29,"totalLines":29,"truncated":false}},"title":"workspace/in/db/schema.sql","time":{"start":1788191101888,"end":1788191101908}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_0efdc0a084910d3d016a95a17cc83c87d299ef68c97aa955ae"}},"id":"prt_0587ed2a7001O3HANNDgI8j1b6","sessionID":"ses_fa78189c6ffeHzmdRAYto1hSK7","messageID":"msg_0587ebdcc001EkmW35vNF6hgwr"}}
