{"type":"text","timestamp":1788191162782,"sessionID":"ses_fa78189c6ffeHzmdRAYto1hSK7","part":{"id":"prt_0587fbfa2001WKtPeTtMy6ZMFa","messageID":"msg_0587f71fc001n8ohow2fVAPRHQ","sessionID":"ses_fa78189c6ffeHzmdRAYto1hSK7","type":"text","text":"I’m writing the migration and the companion preflight, rollback, postcheck, and migration report files now. The migration uses a transactional rebuild, deterministic email repair, and leaves `orders` in place so `user_id` references remain intact.","time":{"start":1788191162274,"end":1788191162771},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"msg_0b32b697c57ec6b0016a95a1b9fc8487d2acc849ae0e7985e5","phase":"commentary"}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788191198725,"sessionID":"ses_fa78189c6ffeHzmdRAYto1hSK7","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_kLdRRXtAtToadCoZx0Mm9nGe","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Update File: /workspace/in/db/migration.sql\n@@\n-DROP TABLE users;\n-\n-CREATE TABLE users (\n-    id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,\n-    email TEXT UNIQUE,\n-    name TEXT NOT NULL,\n-    status TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'active',\n-    created_at TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP\n-);\n+PRAGMA foreign_keys = OFF;\n+\n+BEGIN TRANSACTION;\n+\n+DROP TABLE IF EXISTS users__migration_backup;\n+DROP TABLE IF EXISTS users__migration_new;\n+\n+CREATE TABLE users__migration_backup AS\n+SELECT\n+    id,\n+    email,\n+    name,\n+    created_at\n+FROM users;\n+\n+CREATE TABLE users__migration_new (\n+    id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,\n+    email TEXT NOT NULL UNIQUE CHECK (trim(email) <> ''),\n+    name TEXT NOT NULL,\n+    status TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'active',\n+    created_at TEXT NOT NULL\n+);\n+\n+-- Preserve every existing user row while deterministically repairing the known\n+-- duplicate, null, and blank legacy emails before enforcing new constraints.\n+INSERT INTO users__migration_new (id, email, name, status, created_at)\n+SELECT\n+    id,\n+    CASE\n+        WHEN id = 'u4' THEN 'ada+u4@example.com'\n+        WHEN id = 'u5' THEN 'missing+u5@example.invalid'\n+        WHEN id = 'u6' THEN 'missing+u6@example.invalid'\n+        WHEN email IS NULL THEN 'missing+' || id || '@example.invalid'\n+        WHEN trim(email) = '' THEN 'missing+' || id || '@example.invalid'\n+        ELSE email\n+    END AS email,\n+    name,\n+    'active' AS status,\n+    created_at\n+FROM users__migration_backup\n+ORDER BY created_at, id;\n+\n+DROP TABLE users;\n+ALTER TABLE users__migration_new RENAME TO users;\n+DROP TABLE users__migration_backup;\n+\n+CREATE UNIQUE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_users_email ON users(email);\n+\n+COMMIT;\n+\n+PRAGMA foreign_keys = ON;\n*** Add File: /workspace/in/db/preflight_report.md\n+# Preflight Report\n+\n+## Dirty user email issues before migration\n+\n+- Duplicate email: `ada@example.com` is used by `u1` and `u4`.\n+- Null email: `u5` has `NULL` in `users.email`.\n+- Blank email: `u6` has an empty-string value in `users.email`.\n+\n+## Dependent orders that must be preserved\n+\n+- `u4` has dependent order `o2`.\n+- `u5` has dependent order `o3`.\n+- `u6` has dependent order `o4`.\n+\n+## Required cleanup mapping\n+\n+- Keep `u1` as `ada@example.com`.\n+- Rewrite `u4` to `ada+u4@example.com`.\n+- Rewrite `u5` to `missing+u5@example.invalid`.\n+- Rewrite `u6` to `missing+u6@example.invalid`.\n+\n+## Migration risk if handled unsafely\n+\n+- Dropping and recreating `users` without copying data would remove all users.\n+- Rebuilding `users` without preserving ids would break `orders.user_id` references.\n+- Enforcing `NOT NULL` and `UNIQUE` before cleanup would fail on the existing dirty rows.\n*** Add File: /workspace/in/db/rollback.sql\n+PRAGMA foreign_keys = OFF;\n+\n+BEGIN TRANSACTION;\n+\n+DROP TABLE IF EXISTS users__rollback_new;\n+\n+CREATE TABLE users__rollback_new (\n+    id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,\n+    email TEXT,\n+    name TEXT NOT NULL,\n+    created_at TEXT NOT NULL\n+);\n+\n+INSERT INTO users__rollback_new (id, email, name, created_at)\n+SELECT\n+    id,\n+    email,\n+    name,\n+    created_at\n+FROM users\n+ORDER BY created_at, id;\n+\n+DROP TABLE users;\n+ALTER TABLE users__rollback_new RENAME TO users;\n+\n+COMMIT;\n+\n+PRAGMA foreign_keys = ON;\n*** Add File: /workspace/in/db/postcheck.sql\n+SELECT 'user_row_count' AS check_name, COUNT(*) AS actual_count, 6 AS expected_count\n+FROM users;\n+\n+SELECT 'order_row_count' AS check_name, COUNT(*) AS actual_count, 4 AS expected_count\n+FROM orders;\n+\n+SELECT 'dirty_user_orders_preserved' AS check_name, user_id, GROUP_CONCAT(id, ',') AS order_ids, COUNT(*) AS order_count\n+FROM orders\n+WHERE user_id IN ('u4', 'u5', 'u6')\n+GROUP BY user_id\n+ORDER BY user_id;\n+\n+SELECT 'dirty_user_email_cleanup' AS check_name, id, email\n+FROM users\n+WHERE id IN ('u4', 'u5', 'u6')\n+ORDER BY id;\n+\n+SELECT 'null_or_blank_email_count' AS check_name, COUNT(*) AS invalid_email_count, 0 AS expected_count\n+FROM users\n+WHERE email IS NULL OR trim(email) = '';\n+\n+SELECT 'duplicate_email_group_count' AS check_name, COUNT(*) AS duplicate_group_count, 0 AS expected_count\n+FROM (\n+    SELECT email\n+    FROM users\n+    GROUP BY email\n+    HAVING COUNT(*) > 1\n+);\n+\n+SELECT 'status_null_or_non_active_count' AS check_name, COUNT(*) AS invalid_status_count, 0 AS expected_count\n+FROM users\n+WHERE status IS NULL OR trim(status) = '' OR status <> 'active';\n+\n+SELECT 'users_status_column' AS check_name, name, type, \"notnull\", dflt_value\n+FROM pragma_table_info('users')\n+WHERE name = 'status';\n+\n+SELECT 'users_table_definition' AS check_name, sql\n+FROM sqlite_schema\n+WHERE type = 'table' AND name = 'users';\n*** Add File: /workspace/in/db/migration_report.md\n+# Migration Report\n+\n+## Strategy\n+\n+- Run the migration inside an explicit transaction with foreign keys temporarily disabled during the table swap.\n+- Copy the current `users` rows into a backup table.\n+- Rebuild `users` with the new schema: `id`, `email`, `name`, `status`, `created_at`.\n+- Reinsert every existing user with the original `id`, `name`, and `created_at` so dependent `orders.user_id` values remain valid.\n+- Replace the old `users` table only after the cleaned data has been inserted successfully.\n+\n+## Dirty-data cleanup\n+\n+- Keep the original `ada@example.com` row unchanged for `u1`.\n+- Rewrite `u4` to `ada+u4@example.com`.\n+- Rewrite `u5` to `missing+u5@example.invalid`.\n+- Rewrite `u6` to `missing+u6@example.invalid`.\n+- The rebuilt schema enforces `email TEXT NOT NULL UNIQUE CHECK (trim(email) <> '')` for future writes.\n+- The migration sets `status` to `active` for all existing rows and preserves historical `created_at` values.\n+\n+## Idempotency approach\n+\n+- The script always rebuilds `users` from the current table contents rather than appending rows, so rerunning it does not duplicate data.\n+- The cleanup mapping is deterministic, so `u4`, `u5`, and `u6` receive the same migrated email values on every run.\n+- The temporary migration tables are dropped with `IF EXISTS` before reuse so leftover artifacts do not break a second execution.\n+\n+## Rollback behavior and limitation\n+\n+- `rollback.sql` restores the pre-migration `users` schema shape to `id`, `email`, `name`, `created_at`.\n+- Rollback preserves the same number of users and orders, and keeps the same user ids so order references remain intact.\n+- Rollback does not recreate the original dirty email values; it keeps the migrated email values while removing the `status` column and email constraints.\n+\n+## Postcheck queries\n+\n+Run `postcheck.sql` after the migration to verify:\n+\n+- user row count remains `6`\n+- order row count remains `4`\n+- orders for `u4`, `u5`, and `u6` are still present\n+- cleaned email values were applied to `u4`, `u5`, and `u6`\n+- no null, blank, or duplicate emails remain\n+- the `status` column exists with `NOT NULL` and default `active`\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nM workspace/in/db/migration.sql\nA workspace/in/db/preflight_report.md\nA workspace/in/db/rollback.sql\nA workspace/in/db/postcheck.sql\nA workspace/in/db/migration_report.md","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /workspace/in/db/migration.sql\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/in/db/migration.sql\n+++ /workspace/in/db/migration.sql\n@@ -1,9 +1,51 @@\n-DROP TABLE users;\n+PRAGMA foreign_keys = OFF;\n \n-CREATE TABLE users (\n+BEGIN TRANSACTION;\n+\n+DROP TABLE IF EXISTS users__migration_backup;\n+DROP TABLE IF EXISTS users__migration_new;\n+\n+CREATE TABLE users__migration_backup AS\n+SELECT\n+    id,\n+    email,\n+    name,\n+    created_at\n+FROM users;\n+\n+CREATE TABLE users__migration_new (\n     id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,\n-    email TEXT UNIQUE,\n+    email TEXT NOT NULL UNIQUE CHECK (trim(email) <> ''),\n     name TEXT NOT NULL,\n     status TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'active',\n-    created_at TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP\n+    created_at TEXT NOT NULL\n );\n+\n+-- Preserve every existing user row while deterministically repairing the known\n+-- duplicate, null, and blank legacy emails before enforcing new constraints.\n+INSERT INTO users__migration_new (id, email, name, status, created_at)\n+SELECT\n+    id,\n+    CASE\n+        WHEN id = 'u4' THEN 'ada+u4@example.com'\n+        WHEN id = 'u5' THEN 'missing+u5@example.invalid'\n+        WHEN id = 'u6' THEN 'missing+u6@example.invalid'\n+        WHEN email IS NULL THEN 'missing+' || id || '@example.invalid'\n+        WHEN trim(email) = '' THEN 'missing+' || id || '@example.invalid'\n+        ELSE email\n+    END AS email,\n+    name,\n+    'active' AS status,\n+    created_at\n+FROM users__migration_backup\n+ORDER BY created_at, id;\n+\n+DROP TABLE users;\n+ALTER TABLE users__migration_new RENAME TO users;\n+DROP TABLE users__migration_backup;\n+\n+CREATE UNIQUE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_users_email ON users(email);\n+\n+COMMIT;\n+\n+PRAGMA foreign_keys = ON;\n\nIndex: /workspace/in/db/preflight_report.md\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/in/db/preflight_report.md\n+++ /workspace/in/db/preflight_report.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,26 @@\n+# Preflight Report\n+\n+## Dirty user email issues before migration\n+\n+- Duplicate email: `ada@example.com` is used by `u1` and `u4`.\n+- Null email: `u5` has `NULL` in `users.email`.\n+- Blank email: `u6` has an empty-string value in `users.email`.\n+\n+## Dependent orders that must be preserved\n+\n+- `u4` has dependent order `o2`.\n+- `u5` has dependent order `o3`.\n+- `u6` has dependent order `o4`.\n+\n+## Required cleanup mapping\n+\n+- Keep `u1` as `ada@example.com`.\n+- Rewrite `u4` to `ada+u4@example.com`.\n+- Rewrite `u5` to `missing+u5@example.invalid`.\n+- Rewrite `u6` to `missing+u6@example.invalid`.\n+\n+## Migration risk if handled unsafely\n+\n+- Dropping and recreating `users` without copying data would remove all users.\n+- Rebuilding `users` without preserving ids would break `orders.user_id` references.\n+- Enforcing `NOT NULL` and `UNIQUE` before cleanup would fail on the existing dirty rows.\n\nIndex: /workspace/in/db/rollback.sql\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/in/db/rollback.sql\n+++ /workspace/in/db/rollback.sql\n@@ -0,0 +1,28 @@\n+PRAGMA foreign_keys = OFF;\n+\n+BEGIN TRANSACTION;\n+\n+DROP TABLE IF EXISTS users__rollback_new;\n+\n+CREATE TABLE users__rollback_new (\n+    id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,\n+    email TEXT,\n+    name TEXT NOT NULL,\n+    created_at TEXT NOT NULL\n+);\n+\n+INSERT INTO users__rollback_new (id, email, name, created_at)\n+SELECT\n+    id,\n+    email,\n+    name,\n+    created_at\n+FROM users\n+ORDER BY created_at, id;\n+\n+DROP TABLE users;\n+ALTER TABLE users__rollback_new RENAME TO users;\n+\n+COMMIT;\n+\n+PRAGMA foreign_keys = ON;\n\nIndex: /workspace/in/db/postcheck.sql\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/in/db/postcheck.sql\n+++ /workspace/in/db/postcheck.sql\n@@ -0,0 +1,40 @@\n+SELECT 'user_row_count' AS check_name, COUNT(*) AS actual_count, 6 AS expected_count\n+FROM users;\n+\n+SELECT 'order_row_count' AS check_name, COUNT(*) AS actual_count, 4 AS expected_count\n+FROM orders;\n+\n+SELECT 'dirty_user_orders_preserved' AS check_name, user_id, GROUP_CONCAT(id, ',') AS order_ids, COUNT(*) AS order_count\n+FROM orders\n+WHERE user_id IN ('u4', 'u5', 'u6')\n+GROUP BY user_id\n+ORDER BY user_id;\n+\n+SELECT 'dirty_user_email_cleanup' AS check_name, id, email\n+FROM users\n+WHERE id IN ('u4', 'u5', 'u6')\n+ORDER BY id;\n+\n+SELECT 'null_or_blank_email_count' AS check_name, COUNT(*) AS invalid_email_count, 0 AS expected_count\n+FROM users\n+WHERE email IS NULL OR trim(email) = '';\n+\n+SELECT 'duplicate_email_group_count' AS check_name, COUNT(*) AS duplicate_group_count, 0 AS expected_count\n+FROM (\n+    SELECT email\n+    FROM users\n+    GROUP BY email\n+    HAVING COUNT(*) > 1\n+);\n+\n+SELECT 'status_null_or_non_active_count' AS check_name, COUNT(*) AS invalid_status_count, 0 AS expected_count\n+FROM users\n+WHERE status IS NULL OR trim(status) = '' OR status <> 'active';\n+\n+SELECT 'users_status_column' AS check_name, name, type, \"notnull\", dflt_value\n+FROM pragma_table_info('users')\n+WHERE name = 'status';\n+\n+SELECT 'users_table_definition' AS check_name, sql\n+FROM sqlite_schema\n+WHERE type = 'table' AND name = 'users';\n\nIndex: /workspace/in/db/migration_report.md\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/in/db/migration_report.md\n+++ /workspace/in/db/migration_report.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,41 @@\n+# Migration Report\n+\n+## Strategy\n+\n+- Run the migration inside an explicit transaction with foreign keys temporarily disabled during the table swap.\n+- Copy the current `users` rows into a backup table.\n+- Rebuild `users` with the new schema: `id`, `email`, `name`, `status`, `created_at`.\n+- Reinsert every existing user with the original `id`, `name`, and `created_at` so dependent `orders.user_id` values remain valid.\n+- Replace the old `users` table only after the cleaned data has been inserted successfully.\n+\n+## Dirty-data cleanup\n+\n+- Keep the original `ada@example.com` row unchanged for `u1`.\n+- Rewrite `u4` to `ada+u4@example.com`.\n+- Rewrite `u5` to `missing+u5@example.invalid`.\n+- Rewrite `u6` to `missing+u6@example.invalid`.\n+- The rebuilt schema enforces `email TEXT NOT NULL UNIQUE CHECK (trim(email) <> '')` for future writes.\n+- The migration sets `status` to `active` for all existing rows and preserves historical `created_at` values.\n+\n+## Idempotency approach\n+\n+- The script always rebuilds `users` from the current table contents rather than appending rows, so rerunning it does not duplicate data.\n+- The cleanup mapping is deterministic, so `u4`, `u5`, and `u6` receive the same migrated email values on every run.\n+- The temporary migration tables are dropped with `IF EXISTS` before reuse so leftover artifacts do not break a second execution.\n+\n+## Rollback behavior and limitation\n+\n+- `rollback.sql` restores the pre-migration `users` schema shape to `id`, `email`, `name`, `created_at`.\n+- Rollback preserves the same number of users and orders, and keeps the same user ids so order references remain intact.\n+- Rollback does not recreate the original dirty email values; it keeps the migrated email values while removing the `status` column and email constraints.\n+\n+## Postcheck queries\n+\n+Run `postcheck.sql` after the migration to verify:\n+\n+- user row count remains `6`\n+- order row count remains `4`\n+- orders for `u4`, `u5`, and `u6` are still present\n+- cleaned email values were applied to `u4`, `u5`, and `u6`\n+- no null, blank, or duplicate emails remain\n+- the `status` column exists with `NOT NULL` and default `active`\n\n","files":[{"filePath":"/workspace/in/db/migration.sql","relativePath":"workspace/in/db/migration.sql","type":"update","patch":"Index: /workspace/in/db/migration.sql\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/in/db/migration.sql\n+++ /workspace/in/db/migration.sql\n@@ -1,9 +1,51 @@\n-DROP TABLE users;\n+PRAGMA foreign_keys = OFF;\n \n-CREATE TABLE users (\n+BEGIN TRANSACTION;\n+\n+DROP TABLE IF EXISTS users__migration_backup;\n+DROP TABLE IF EXISTS users__migration_new;\n+\n+CREATE TABLE users__migration_backup AS\n+SELECT\n+    id,\n+    email,\n+    name,\n+    created_at\n+FROM users;\n+\n+CREATE TABLE users__migration_new (\n     id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,\n-    email TEXT UNIQUE,\n+    email TEXT NOT NULL UNIQUE CHECK (trim(email) <> ''),\n     name TEXT NOT NULL,\n     status TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'active',\n-    created_at TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP\n+    created_at TEXT NOT NULL\n );\n+\n+-- Preserve every existing user row while deterministically repairing the known\n+-- duplicate, null, and blank legacy emails before enforcing new constraints.\n+INSERT INTO users__migration_new (id, email, name, status, created_at)\n+SELECT\n+    id,\n+    CASE\n+        WHEN id = 'u4' THEN 'ada+u4@example.com'\n+        WHEN id = 'u5' THEN 'missing+u5@example.invalid'\n+        WHEN id = 'u6' THEN 'missing+u6@example.invalid'\n+        WHEN email IS NULL THEN 'missing+' || id || '@example.invalid'\n+        WHEN trim(email) = '' THEN 'missing+' || id || '@example.invalid'\n+        ELSE email\n+    END AS email,\n+    name,\n+    'active' AS status,\n+    created_at\n+FROM users__migration_backup\n+ORDER BY created_at, id;\n+\n+DROP TABLE users;\n+ALTER TABLE users__migration_new RENAME TO users;\n+DROP TABLE users__migration_backup;\n+\n+CREATE UNIQUE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_users_email ON users(email);\n+\n+COMMIT;\n+\n+PRAGMA foreign_keys = ON;\n","additions":46,"deletions":4},{"filePath":"/workspace/in/db/preflight_report.md","relativePath":"workspace/in/db/preflight_report.md","type":"add","patch":"Index: /workspace/in/db/preflight_report.md\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/in/db/preflight_report.md\n+++ /workspace/in/db/preflight_report.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,26 @@\n+# Preflight Report\n+\n+## Dirty user email issues before migration\n+\n+- Duplicate email: `ada@example.com` is used by `u1` and `u4`.\n+- Null email: `u5` has `NULL` in `users.email`.\n+- Blank email: `u6` has an empty-string value in `users.email`.\n+\n+## Dependent orders that must be preserved\n+\n+- `u4` has dependent order `o2`.\n+- `u5` has dependent order `o3`.\n+- `u6` has dependent order `o4`.\n+\n+## Required cleanup mapping\n+\n+- Keep `u1` as `ada@example.com`.\n+- Rewrite `u4` to `ada+u4@example.com`.\n+- Rewrite `u5` to `missing+u5@example.invalid`.\n+- Rewrite `u6` to `missing+u6@example.invalid`.\n+\n+## Migration risk if handled unsafely\n+\n+- Dropping and recreating `users` without copying data would remove all users.\n+- Rebuilding `users` without preserving ids would break `orders.user_id` references.\n+- Enforcing `NOT NULL` and `UNIQUE` before cleanup would fail on the existing dirty rows.\n","additions":26,"deletions":0},{"filePath":"/workspace/in/db/rollback.sql","relativePath":"workspace/in/db/rollback.sql","type":"add","patch":"Index: /workspace/in/db/rollback.sql\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/in/db/rollback.sql\n+++ /workspace/in/db/rollback.sql\n@@ -0,0 +1,28 @@\n+PRAGMA foreign_keys = OFF;\n+\n+BEGIN TRANSACTION;\n+\n+DROP TABLE IF EXISTS users__rollback_new;\n+\n+CREATE TABLE users__rollback_new (\n+    id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,\n+    email TEXT,\n+    name TEXT NOT NULL,\n+    created_at TEXT NOT NULL\n+);\n+\n+INSERT INTO users__rollback_new (id, email, name, created_at)\n+SELECT\n+    id,\n+    email,\n+    name,\n+    created_at\n+FROM users\n+ORDER BY created_at, id;\n+\n+DROP TABLE users;\n+ALTER TABLE users__rollback_new RENAME TO users;\n+\n+COMMIT;\n+\n+PRAGMA foreign_keys = ON;\n","additions":28,"deletions":0},{"filePath":"/workspace/in/db/postcheck.sql","relativePath":"workspace/in/db/postcheck.sql","type":"add","patch":"Index: /workspace/in/db/postcheck.sql\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/in/db/postcheck.sql\n+++ /workspace/in/db/postcheck.sql\n@@ -0,0 +1,40 @@\n+SELECT 'user_row_count' AS check_name, COUNT(*) AS actual_count, 6 AS expected_count\n+FROM users;\n+\n+SELECT 'order_row_count' AS check_name, COUNT(*) AS actual_count, 4 AS expected_count\n+FROM orders;\n+\n+SELECT 'dirty_user_orders_preserved' AS check_name, user_id, GROUP_CONCAT(id, ',') AS order_ids, COUNT(*) AS order_count\n+FROM orders\n+WHERE user_id IN ('u4', 'u5', 'u6')\n+GROUP BY user_id\n+ORDER BY user_id;\n+\n+SELECT 'dirty_user_email_cleanup' AS check_name, id, email\n+FROM users\n+WHERE id IN ('u4', 'u5', 'u6')\n+ORDER BY id;\n+\n+SELECT 'null_or_blank_email_count' AS check_name, COUNT(*) AS invalid_email_count, 0 AS expected_count\n+FROM users\n+WHERE email IS NULL OR trim(email) = '';\n+\n+SELECT 'duplicate_email_group_count' AS check_name, COUNT(*) AS duplicate_group_count, 0 AS expected_count\n+FROM (\n+    SELECT email\n+    FROM users\n+    GROUP BY email\n+    HAVING COUNT(*) > 1\n+);\n+\n+SELECT 'status_null_or_non_active_count' AS check_name, COUNT(*) AS invalid_status_count, 0 AS expected_count\n+FROM users\n+WHERE status IS NULL OR trim(status) = '' OR status <> 'active';\n+\n+SELECT 'users_status_column' AS check_name, name, type, \"notnull\", dflt_value\n+FROM pragma_table_info('users')\n+WHERE name = 'status';\n+\n+SELECT 'users_table_definition' AS check_name, sql\n+FROM sqlite_schema\n+WHERE type = 'table' AND name = 'users';\n","additions":40,"deletions":0},{"filePath":"/workspace/in/db/migration_report.md","relativePath":"workspace/in/db/migration_report.md","type":"add","patch":"Index: /workspace/in/db/migration_report.md\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/in/db/migration_report.md\n+++ /workspace/in/db/migration_report.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,41 @@\n+# Migration Report\n+\n+## Strategy\n+\n+- Run the migration inside an explicit transaction with foreign keys temporarily disabled during the table swap.\n+- Copy the current `users` rows into a backup table.\n+- Rebuild `users` with the new schema: `id`, `email`, `name`, `status`, `created_at`.\n+- Reinsert every existing user with the original `id`, `name`, and `created_at` so dependent `orders.user_id` values remain valid.\n+- Replace the old `users` table only after the cleaned data has been inserted successfully.\n+\n+## Dirty-data cleanup\n+\n+- Keep the original `ada@example.com` row unchanged for `u1`.\n+- Rewrite `u4` to `ada+u4@example.com`.\n+- Rewrite `u5` to `missing+u5@example.invalid`.\n+- Rewrite `u6` to `missing+u6@example.invalid`.\n+- The rebuilt schema enforces `email TEXT NOT NULL UNIQUE CHECK (trim(email) <> '')` for future writes.\n+- The migration sets `status` to `active` for all existing rows and preserves historical `created_at` values.\n+\n+## Idempotency approach\n+\n+- The script always rebuilds `users` from the current table contents rather than appending rows, so rerunning it does not duplicate data.\n+- The cleanup mapping is deterministic, so `u4`, `u5`, and `u6` receive the same migrated email values on every run.\n+- The temporary migration tables are dropped with `IF EXISTS` before reuse so leftover artifacts do not break a second execution.\n+\n+## Rollback behavior and limitation\n+\n+- `rollback.sql` restores the pre-migration `users` schema shape to `id`, `email`, `name`, `created_at`.\n+- Rollback preserves the same number of users and orders, and keeps the same user ids so order references remain intact.\n+- Rollback does not recreate the original dirty email values; it keeps the migrated email values while removing the `status` column and email constraints.\n+\n+## Postcheck queries\n+\n+Run `postcheck.sql` after the migration to verify:\n+\n+- user row count remains `6`\n+- order row count remains `4`\n+- orders for `u4`, `u5`, and `u6` are still present\n+- cleaned email values were applied to `u4`, `u5`, and `u6`\n+- no null, blank, or duplicate emails remain\n+- the `status` column exists with `NOT NULL` and default `active`\n","additions":41,"deletions":0}],"diagnostics":{},"truncated":false},"title":"Success. Updated the following files:\nM workspace/in/db/migration.sql\nA workspace/in/db/preflight_report.md\nA workspace/in/db/rollback.sql\nA workspace/in/db/postcheck.sql\nA workspace/in/db/migration_report.md","time":{"start":1788191198686,"end":1788191198715}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_0b32b697c57ec6b0016a95a1baa46887d2b044df5739fd717a"}},"id":"prt_0587fc199001GBhsmGQ9b6Pefq","sessionID":"ses_fa78189c6ffeHzmdRAYto1hSK7","messageID":"msg_0587f71fc001n8ohow2fVAPRHQ"}}
