{"type":"text","timestamp":1788191224878,"sessionID":"ses_fa78189c6ffeHzmdRAYto1hSK7","part":{"id":"prt_05880a48a001hhlg2UBTmi35Y3","messageID":"msg_058809da1001M6vHhMhfpKZC1h","sessionID":"ses_fa78189c6ffeHzmdRAYto1hSK7","type":"text","text":"Updated these files under `/workspace/in/db`:\n\n- `migration.sql`\n- `preflight_report.md`\n- `rollback.sql`\n- `postcheck.sql`\n- `migration_report.md`\n\nWhat changed:\n\n- Replaced the destructive migration with a transactional table rebuild.\n- Preserved all `users.id`, `users.name`, `users.created_at`, and existing `orders.user_id` references.\n- Added `users.status TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'active'`.\n- Enforced future email validity with `email TEXT NOT NULL UNIQUE CHECK (trim(email) <> '')`.\n- Applied the required deterministic cleanup:\n  - `u4` -> `ada+u4@example.com`\n  - `u5` -> `missing+u5@example.invalid`\n  - `u6` -> `missing+u6@example.invalid`\n- Added a rollback script that restores the old `users` schema shape.\n- Added preflight and postcheck documentation/queries.\n\nConstraint:\n- I could not execute the SQL locally because `sqlite3` is not installed in this environment. I did a consistency review of the scripts, but not a live run.","time":{"start":1788191220874,"end":1788191224873},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"msg_05043a3ab19bcf72016a95a1f4c7f087d29547be8f3ae5bba7","phase":"final_answer"}}}}
